course: dictionary
lesson: 16006
title: Vanity: pride, emptiness and dressing tables
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Vanity means being too proud of how you look or what you can do. A person full of vanity cares too much about being admired. «Sam spent all morning in front of the mirror, combing his hair and asking everyone if he looked handsome.» The clue is that he cares more about his looks than anything else, so the word is vanity.
explain: Books show vanity through what characters say. «Toad» in The Wind in the Willows sings songs about how great he is: «The world has held great Heroes … but never a name to go down to fame compared with that of Toad!» Toad is praising himself, which shows his vanity.
explain: Vanity has two more meanings. In old Bible language, «vanity of vanities, all is vanity» means that everything in this life is empty and passes away. A vanity can also be a cupboard under a bathroom basin, or a dressing table.
fact: Vanity means being too proud of how you look or what you can do.
fact: In old Bible language, vanity means something worthless or empty, as in «vanity of vanities, all is vanity».
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is full of vanity and sings songs praising himself.
fact: In the fable of the crow and the fox, the crow's vanity makes it drop the cheese.
fact: A bathroom vanity is a cupboard under the basin, or a dressing table.
exercise: «Sam spent all morning admiring himself in the mirror and asking everyone if he looked handsome.» What does this show? | Hunger | *Vanity | Kindness | Fear
exercise: In the fable, why does the crow drop the cheese? | It is hungry and wants to sleep | *It is so proud of its voice that it opens its beak to sing | It is scared of the fox | It wants to give the cheese away
exercise: In the Bible sentence «vanity of vanities, all is vanity», what does vanity mean? | Being very loud | Being kind and generous | A cupboard in the bathroom | *Something worthless or empty
test: «Lily kept telling everyone how pretty she looked in her new dress, and she checked her reflection every minute.» Lily is showing | *Vanity | Bravery | Hunger | Sleepiness
test: What is a vanity in a bathroom? | A bath towel | A kind of shower | *A cupboard under the basin, or a dressing table | A type of soap
exam: Toad sings «never a name to go down to fame compared with that of Toad!» What does this show about Toad? | Tiredness | *Vanity, because he praises himself | Shyness | Anger at the river
